From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 06:41:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winhttp: let a request's autologon policy be read back.

WINHTTP_OPTION_AUTOLOGON_POLICY can be set on a request -- request_set_option
stores it on the object header -- and querying it fell through to the default
case, which logs a FIXME and answers ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER. An option that
can be set and not got is a shape no caller expects, and the value was already
sitting there waiting to be returned.

Seen because Office asks for it twice while signing in, from two threads, and
Word then raised an unhandled 0x1e044000 and vanished twenty-seven seconds into
start-up. Whether the failed query is what Office fails fast on is not proven
-- the crash has been seen once -- but the option is wrong on its own terms and
the FIXME is gone after this.

(cherry picked from commit 04bb4aa44893ddc62ab7acda3784b64b84609ba2)

diff --git a/dlls/winhttp/session.c b/dlls/winhttp/session.c
index 68f8ee98ede..0fb35f99250 100644
--- a/dlls/winhttp/session.c
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/session.c
@@ -866,6 +866,18 @@ static BOOL request_query_option( struct object_header *hdr, DWORD option, void
 
     switch (option)
     {
+    /* AUTOLOGON_POLICY is settable on a request and could not be read back.
+     * request_set_option stores it on the object header; the query side fell
+     * through to the default case, which answers ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER. An
+     * option that can be set and not got is a shape no caller expects, and
+     * Office asks for this one while signing in. */
+    case WINHTTP_OPTION_AUTOLOGON_POLICY:
+        if (!validate_buffer( buffer, buflen, sizeof(DWORD) )) return FALSE;
+
+        *(DWORD *)buffer = hdr->logon_policy;
+        *buflen = sizeof(DWORD);
+        return TRUE;
+
     case WINHTTP_OPTION_PARENT_HANDLE:
     {
         if (!validate_buffer( buffer, buflen, sizeof(HINTERNET) )) return FALSE;
